# Testing

`gleam test` runs every **`pub`** function whose name ends in `_test` in
any module under `test/`. A test fails when it panics. Tests mirror the
code: the test for `src/{{.Name}}/features/notes/notes_controller.gleam`
is `test/{{.Name}}/features/notes/notes_controller_test.gleam`.

Run one quickly with `gleam test`, then the whole check with `howdy check`.

## Shape of a test

```gleam
import gleam/http/response
import gleam/string
import howdy/testing
import {{.Name}}/support

pub fn lists_notes_test() {
{{- if .Database}}
  use db <- support.with_db()            // a fresh, migrated database for this test
  let res = testing.get("/api/notes") |> testing.send(support.app(db))
{{- else}}
  let res = testing.get("/health") |> testing.send(support.app())
{{- end}}
  assert res.status == 200
  assert response.get_header(res, "content-type")
    == Ok("application/json; charset=utf-8")
}
```

Assert with the `assert` keyword and `let assert` patterns, as the
generated tests do, not gleeunit's `should`:

```gleam
let assert Ok(item) = testing.json(res, note.decoder())
assert item.body == "Hello"
let assert Ok([error]) = testing.field_errors(res)
assert error.field == "body"
```

`test/{{.Name}}/support.gleam` builds the app with the services it gets at
startup{{if .Database}}, and `support.with_db` gives each test its own {{if eq .Database "postgres"}}empty test database (`TEST_DATABASE_URL`; start PostgreSQL with `docker compose up -d`){{else}}in-memory SQLite
database{{end}}. Add shared helpers there{{end}}.

## howdy/testing

Requests:

| Function | Makes |
| --- | --- |
| `testing.get(path)`, `testing.delete(path)` | a request with no body; `"?a=b"` in the path is the query |
| `testing.post(path, json)`, `put`, `patch` | a JSON request (`json.object([...])`) |
| `testing.post_form(path, [#("name", "value")])` | a form post |
| `testing.request(http.Put, path)` | any method, then add a body |
| `\|> testing.form_body(pairs)`, `json_body(j)`, `text_body(s)`, `bytes_body(b)` | a body on a request |
| `\|> testing.header(name, value)`, `query(pairs)`, `cookie(name, value)`, `from_ip(ip)` | headers and the rest |

Send with `|> testing.send(app)`, then read the response:

| Function | Gives |
| --- | --- |
| `res.status` | the status code |
| `response.get_header(res, "location")` | a header (`gleam/http/response`) |
| `testing.text(res)` | the body as a String |
| `testing.json(res, decoder)` | the decoded JSON body |
| `testing.error(res)` | the `"error"` message of an error response |
| `testing.field_errors(res)` | the field errors of a 422 |
| `testing.cookies(res)` | cookies set, as `#(name, value)` |

There is no helper for a POST without a body (`testing.request(http.Post, path)`),
for PUT or PATCH with a form (`testing.request(http.Put, path) |> testing.form_body(pairs)`)
or for HTML: check it with `string.contains(testing.text(res), "...")`.

## What to test

- Each route's success case, with the status and the body.
- Each validation rule: send a bad value, expect 422 and the field.
- Missing records: 404. Guarded routes: 401 without credentials.
{{- if .Database}}
- Database operations directly, without HTTP: build input through the
  record's `validate` (the only way to make a `NewX`), then call the
  operations module:

  ```gleam
  pub fn finds_by_email_test() {
    use db <- support.with_db()
    let assert Ok(input) = user.validate(user.UserInput(name: "Ada", email: "ada@example.com"))
    let assert Ok(created) = users.create(db, input)
    assert users.find_by_email(db, "ada@example.com") == Ok(created)
  }
  ```

- Records a test only needs to exist: insert them with the record's factory
  in `dev/{{.Name}}/factories/`, which validates them the same way:
  `user_factory.insert(db, UserInput(..user_factory.input(), email: "ada@example.com"))`,
  or `user_factory.insert_many(db, 3, fn(input) { input })`.
{{- end}}
{{- if not .API}}
- Pages: status 200, `content-type` `text/html; charset=utf-8`, and text
  that should be on the page. A form post that succeeds answers 303 with a
  `location` header; one that fails validation answers 422 and shows the
  form again.
- Live routes answer 426 without a WebSocket; test a live view's `update`
  and `view` functions directly instead.
{{- end}}

## Guarded routes

Once the project has auth (`howdy add auth`), the generators give
`support.sign_in(db)`, which returns a session token. Call it **once per
database** (a second call conflicts on the same email) and send it as a
bearer token:

```gleam
let token = support.sign_in(db)
let send = fn(req) {
  req
  |> testing.header("authorization", "Bearer " <> token)
  |> testing.send(app)
}
```

## When a test fails

Read the assertion in the output: it shows both sides. `testing.text(res)`
of a failing response usually says why (`{"error":...}`). A test that
passes alone but fails with others is sharing state{{if .Database}}: give it its own
`support.with_db`{{end}}.
